// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//! gpio.resource's functions: who holds which of the chip's pads. A driver
//! takes each pad it routes and gives it back when it is done, so two of
//! them wanting one pad is a refusal at the take rather than a line two
//! drivers fight over. A resource: no Open or Close, its first function in
//! the first slot. The base comes from OpenResource("gpio.resource").
##include resources/gpio as gpio
##basetype GpioBase
##name gpio.resource
##bias 0
##public
/// Take `pad` for `name`, which must outlive the claim: null if it is now
/// yours, else who has it. Not from interrupts.
?[*:0]const u8 AllocGPIO(u32 pad, [*:0]const u8 name)
/// Give `pad` back. Its setting is left as it is. Not from interrupts.
void FreeGPIO(u32 pad)
/// Who holds `pad`, or null if nobody does.
?[*:0]const u8 GPIOOwner(u32 pad)
##end
